IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `mc15-nouns`
IMPORT `mc15-ch01`
IMPORT `mc15-ch02-08`
IMPORT `mc15-ch09-11`
IMPORT `mc15-ch12-16`
IMPORT `mc15-ch17-19`
IMPORT `mc15-ch20-22`
IMPORT `mc15-ch23-32`
IMPORT `mc15-ch33-38`
IMPORT `mc15-ch39-40`
IMPORT `mc15-ch41-42`
IMPORT `mc15-ch43-48`
IMPORT `mc15-ch49-59`
IMPORT `mc15-ch60-63`

-- Magna Carta (1215), English translation in McKechnie 1905 -- THE SEAT LAYER.
--
-- SEAT: a person living under King John's rule who is not the King: a free man, a widow, an heir,
-- a merchant, a tenant who holds land by military service, someone who owes money.  The person asks,
-- on facts they can state, what the Crown and its officers may and may not do to them under the
-- Charter, and what the Charter gives them.  Nothing here is new law, and nothing here says that the
-- Charter was, or is, in force or applied: the questions ask what the text provides.
--
-- PLAIN INPUTS.  Every question takes plain inputs -- yes/no, numbers, a date as day, month and year,
-- and the modules' own choices -- one for each fact the person can state, each with an @desc worded
-- as the person would be asked.  The records and dates the modules expect are built inside each
-- question, in its WHERE, from those answers, and the SAME module rule is then called; no rule is
-- restated here.  Where the text leaves a judgment open (reasonable, lawful, just, evil, credible),
-- the person states it as a fact.
--
-- ANSWERS.  Barred, Entitled and Obliged: the text's own words say so on those facts.  Not barred,
-- Not entitled and Not obliged: the text itself says no in its own words -- a condition it introduces
-- with "if", "only if", "as long as" or "unless" (or their plain variants), a limit it closes with
-- "only" or "nothing but", or a definition that says "means"; each such branch in the chapter modules
-- quotes the words.  Bar not covered, Entitlement not covered and Obligation not covered: the text is
-- silent on those facts, its list is not closed, a term is undefined, or it points outside itself.
-- A question that can answer no is named for its chapter ("Under chapter 9, ..."): the answer is
-- about that chapter and says nothing about any other law.  Where the answer is a number, a date or
-- a choice, the text's own term is used.
--
-- The text names no one who must act in many places (it says "shall be restored", "shall be
-- assigned"); those questions still have answers, and NOTES.md (fork register) says who the text
-- leaves unnamed.  There is no seat for an official: provisions that address only the King's own
-- acts are in the chapter modules, and are here only for what they mean to the person.

§ `Magna Carta (1215) -- the questions of a person under the King`

§§ `The liberties the Charter grants (chapter 1)`

-- Chapter 1.  "Freeman" is the person's own statement; the text does not define it.
@export Under chapter 1, do I hold the liberties this Charter grants?
GIVEN `I am a freeman of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a freeman of the kingdom?
      `I am the heir of a freeman of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are the heir of a freeman of the kingdom?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 1, do I hold the liberties this Charter grants` IS
    `ch 1 -- the person holds the liberties granted in this Charter` `I am a freeman of the kingdom` `I am the heir of a freeman of the kingdom`

§§ `My inheritance, wardship and marriage (chapters 2 to 8)`

-- Chapter 2.  The text does not define relief; the person says whether one is owed.
@export Under chapter 2, do I have my inheritance on paying the ancient relief?
GIVEN `the holder was an earl or a baron` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder was an earl or a baron?
      `the holder held of the King in chief by military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder held of the King in chief by military service?
      `the holder has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder has died?
      `I am of full age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are of full age?
      `I owe a relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you owe a relief?
      `I have paid the ancient relief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have paid the ancient relief?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 2, do I have my inheritance on paying the ancient relief` IS
    `ch 2 -- the heir has his inheritance on payment of the ancient relief` `the holder was an earl or a baron` `the holder held of the King in chief by military service` `the holder has died` `I am of full age` `I owe a relief` `I have paid the ancient relief`

-- Chapter 2.  The money is in the text's units (pounds, shillings).
@export How much relief must I give?
GIVEN `the kind of holding` IS HoldingKind @desc Is it a whole earl's barony, a whole barony or a whole knight's fee?
      `the ancient custom of the fief makes me owe less than the sum the Charter names` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the ancient custom of the fief makes you owe less than the sum the Charter names?
      `the lesser sum owed by custom` IS A NUMBER @desc How much do you owe by custom?  (0 if nothing)
GIVETH A MAYBE Sterling
DECIDE `How much relief must I give` IS
    `ch 2 -- the relief the heir is to give` `the kind of holding` `owed by custom`
    WHERE
        `owed by custom` MEANS IF `the ancient custom of the fief makes me owe less than the sum the Charter names` THEN JUST `the lesser sum owed by custom` ELSE NOTHING

-- Chapter 3.
@export Under chapter 3, may the King demand a relief or a fine from me when I come of age, having been a minor in wardship?
GIVEN `the holder was an earl or a baron` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder was an earl or a baron?
      `the holder held of the King in chief by military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder held of the King in chief by military service?
      `I was a minor in wardship` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were a minor in wardship?
      `I have come of age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have come of age?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 3, may the King demand a relief or a fine from me when I come of age, having been a minor in wardship` IS
    `ch 3 -- relief or a fine may be demanded of the heir on coming of age` `the holder was an earl or a baron` `the holder held of the King in chief by military service` `I was a minor in wardship` `I have come of age`

-- Chapter 4.  "Reasonable" is the person's own statement.
@export Under chapter 4, may my guardian take this from my land?
GIVEN `what is taken is more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that what is taken is more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services?
      `the taking is with destruction or waste of my men or goods` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the taking is with destruction or waste of your men or goods?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 4, may my guardian take this from my land` IS
    `ch 4 -- the guardian may take this from the heir's land` `what is taken is more than reasonable produce, reasonable customs and reasonable services` `the taking is with destruction or waste of my men or goods`

-- Chapter 4.
@export What follows if my guardian lays waste?
GIVEN `how the guardian came to hold the wardship` IS GuardianKind @desc Was the land committed by the King to the sheriff or another accountable to him, or given or sold by the King to someone?
      `the guardian has made destruction or waste` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the guardian has made destruction or waste?
GIVETH A WasteConsequence
DECIDE `What follows if my guardian lays waste` IS
    `ch 4 -- what follows if the guardian lays waste` `how the guardian came to hold the wardship` `the guardian has made destruction or waste`

-- Chapter 5.
@export Under chapter 5, is the restoration of my land what the Charter requires?
GIVEN `all my land is restored` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all your land is restored?
      `it is stocked with ploughs and implements of husbandry` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is stocked with ploughs and implements of husbandry?
      `the stocking is as the season of husbandry requires and the issues of the land can reasonably bear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the stocking is as the season of husbandry requires and the issues of the land can reasonably bear?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 5, is the restoration of my land what the Charter requires` IS
    `ch 5 -- the restoration is what the Charter requires` `all my land is restored` `it is stocked with ploughs and implements of husbandry` `the stocking is as the season of husbandry requires and the issues of the land can reasonably bear`

-- Chapter 6.  "Disparagement" is the person's own statement.
@export Under chapter 6, may I be married in this way?
GIVEN `the marriage is a disparagement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the marriage is a disparagement?
      `my nearest in blood has had notice before the marriage takes place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your nearest in blood has had notice before the marriage takes place?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 6, may I be married in this way` IS
    `ch 6 -- the heir may be married in this way` `the marriage is a disparagement` `my nearest in blood has had notice before the marriage takes place`

-- Chapter 7.
@export Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be kept waiting or put to difficulty over my marriage portion and inheritance?
GIVEN `my husband has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your husband has died?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be kept waiting or put to difficulty over my marriage portion and inheritance` IS
    `ch 7 -- the widow may be kept waiting or put to difficulty over her marriage portion and inheritance` `my husband has died`

-- Chapter 7.
@export Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be made to give anything for my dower, my marriage portion or our inheritance?
GIVEN `my husband has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your husband has died?
      `what is asked of me` IS Demand @desc Is it something for your dower, for your marriage portion, for the inheritance you and your husband held on the day of his death, or some other payment?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, be made to give anything for my dower, my marriage portion or our inheritance` IS
    `ch 7 -- the widow may be made to give this` `my husband has died` `what is asked of me`

-- Chapter 7.  Fork F7b: the day of death is day 0 and day 40 is the last day of the forty.
@export Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, remain in my husband's house?
GIVEN `the days since my husband's death` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days ago did your husband die?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 7, may I, a widow, remain in my husband's house` IS
    `ch 7 -- the widow may remain in her husband's house` `the days since my husband's death`

-- Chapter 7.
@export Under chapter 7, was my dower assigned within the forty days?
GIVEN `the days since my husband's death when my dower was assigned` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days after your husband's death was your dower assigned?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 7, was my dower assigned within the forty days` IS
    `ch 7 -- her dower is assigned within the forty days` `the days since my husband's death when my dower was assigned`

-- Chapter 8.
@export Under chapter 8, may I, a widow, be compelled to marry?
GIVEN `I am a widow` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a widow?
      `I prefer to live without a husband` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you prefer to live without a husband?
      `I give security not to marry without the required consent` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you give security not to marry without the required consent?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 8, may I, a widow, be compelled to marry` IS
    `ch 8 -- the widow may be compelled to marry` `I am a widow` `I prefer to live without a husband` `I give security not to marry without the required consent`

-- Chapter 8.
@export Whose consent does my security against remarrying bind me to?
GIVEN `I hold of the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you hold of the King?
GIVETH A ConsentOf
DECIDE `Whose consent does my security against remarrying bind me to` IS
    `ch 8 -- the consent her security is against` `I hold of the King`

§§ `Debts and sureties (chapters 9 to 11)`

-- Chapter 9.
@export Under chapter 9, may the King or his bailiffs seize my land or rent for my debt?
GIVEN `who would seize it` IS Party @desc Who would seize your land or rent: the King, a bailiff, a sheriff or another?
      `the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 9, may the King or his bailiffs seize my land or rent for my debt` IS
    `ch 9 -- land or rent may be seized for the debt` `who would seize it` `the chattels of the debtor are sufficient to repay the debt`

-- Chapter 9.
@export Under chapter 9, may my sureties be distrained while I am able to pay?
GIVEN `I, the principal debtor, am able to satisfy the debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you, the principal debtor, are able to satisfy the debt?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 9, may my sureties be distrained while I am able to pay` IS
    `ch 9 -- the sureties of the debtor may be distrained` `I, the principal debtor, am able to satisfy the debt`

-- Chapter 9.
@export Under chapter 9, must I, as a surety, answer for the debt?
GIVEN `the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt?
      `the principal debtor has failed to pay the debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the principal debtor has failed to pay the debt?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 9, must I, as a surety, answer for the debt` IS
    `ch 9 -- the sureties answer for the debt` `the principal debtor is able to satisfy the debt` `the principal debtor has failed to pay the debt`

-- Chapter 9.
@export Under chapter 9, may I, a surety who has paid, have the lands and rents of the debtor?
GIVEN `I have paid the debt for the debtor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have paid the debt for the debtor?
      `I desire the lands and rents` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you desire the lands and rents?
      `I have been indemnified for what I paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have been indemnified for what you paid?
      `the principal debtor shows proof that he is discharged as against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the principal debtor shows proof that he is discharged as against you?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 9, may I, a surety who has paid, have the lands and rents of the debtor` IS
    `ch 9 -- the surety may have the lands and rents of the debtor` `I have paid the debt for the debtor` `I desire the lands and rents` `I have been indemnified for what I paid` `the principal debtor shows proof that he is discharged as against me`

-- Chapter 10.  "The Jews" is the text's name for a class of lenders.
@export Under chapter 10, may the debt I owe to the Jews bear interest while the heir is under age?
GIVEN `the loan was borrowed from the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the loan was borrowed from the Jews?
      `the borrower died before the loan was repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the borrower died before the loan was repaid?
      `the heir is under age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the heir is under age?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 10, may the debt I owe to the Jews bear interest while the heir is under age` IS
    `ch 10 -- the debt may bear interest` `the loan was borrowed from the Jews` `the borrower died before the loan was repaid` `the heir is under age`

-- Chapter 10.
@export Under chapter 10, may the King take more than the principal sum of a debt that has fallen into his hands?
GIVEN `the loan was borrowed from the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the loan was borrowed from the Jews?
      `the borrower died before the loan was repaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the borrower died before the loan was repaid?
      `the debt has fallen into the King's hands` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debt has fallen into the King's hands?
      `the principal sum contained in the bond` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the principal sum contained in the bond?
      `the sum the King would take` IS A NUMBER @desc What sum would the King take?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 10, may the King take more than the principal sum of a debt that has fallen into his hands` IS
    `ch 10 -- the King may take this sum of the debt` `the loan was borrowed from the Jews` `the borrower died before the loan was repaid` `the debt has fallen into the King's hands` `the principal sum contained in the bond` `the sum the King would take`

-- Chapter 11, with 11.4.
@export Under chapter 11, do I, as the widow, keep my dower and pay nothing of my husband's debt?
GIVEN `my husband died indebted to the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your husband died indebted to the Jews?
      `my husband died indebted to others than the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your husband died indebted to others than the Jews?
      `I am his wife` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are his wife?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 11, do I, as the widow, keep my dower and pay nothing of my husband's debt` IS
    `ch 11 -- the wife has her dower and pays nothing of the debt` `my husband died indebted to the Jews` `my husband died indebted to others than the Jews` `I am his wife`

-- Chapter 11, with 11.4.
@export Under chapter 11, must necessaries be provided for my children under age?
GIVEN `the deceased died indebted to the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deceased died indebted to the Jews?
      `the deceased died indebted to others than the Jews` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deceased died indebted to others than the Jews?
      `a child of the deceased is left under age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a child of the deceased is left under age?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 11, must necessaries be provided for my children under age` IS
    `ch 11 -- necessaries shall be provided for the children under age, in keeping with the holding of the deceased` `the deceased died indebted to the Jews` `the deceased died indebted to others than the Jews` `a child of the deceased is left under age`

-- Chapter 11.  The text reserves the service due to feudal lords; it is not reduced by this payment.
@export How much of the debt is paid out of what remains after the dower and the necessaries?
GIVEN `the debt` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the debt?
      `the residue after the dower and the necessaries` IS A NUMBER @desc How much remains after the widow's dower and the children's necessaries?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much of the debt is paid out of what remains after the dower and the necessaries` IS
    `ch 11 -- the amount of the debt paid out of the residue` `the debt` `the residue after the dower and the necessaries`

§§ `Taxes and levies (chapters 12 to 16)`

-- Chapter 12.  "Reasonable" is the person's own statement.
@export Under chapter 12, may the King impose this scutage or aid on me?
GIVEN `the kind of levy` IS LevyKind @desc Is it a scutage or an aid?
      `what the levy is for` IS AidPurpose @desc Is it for ransoming the King, making his eldest son a knight, marrying his eldest daughter (once), or some other purpose?
      `an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before?
      `it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom?
      `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the aid is no more than a reasonable aid?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 12, may the King impose this scutage or aid on me` IS
    `ch 12 -- a scutage or aid may be imposed` `the kind of levy` `what the levy is for` `an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before` `it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom` `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid`

-- Chapter 12.
@export Under chapter 12, may an aid be imposed on me, a citizen of London?
GIVEN `what the aid is for` IS AidPurpose @desc Is it for ransoming the King, making his eldest son a knight, marrying his eldest daughter (once), or some other purpose?
      `an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before?
      `it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom?
      `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the aid is no more than a reasonable aid?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 12, may an aid be imposed on me, a citizen of London` IS
    `ch 12 -- an aid from the citizens of London may be imposed` `what the aid is for` `an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before` `it is imposed by the common counsel of the kingdom` `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid`

-- Chapter 13.
@export Under chapter 13, do I, a citizen of London, keep my ancient liberties and free customs?
GIVEN `I am a citizen of London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a citizen of London?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 13, do I, a citizen of London, keep my ancient liberties and free customs` IS
    `ch 13 -- the citizens of London have all their ancient liberties and free customs, by land and by water` `I am a citizen of London`

-- Chapter 13.
@export Under chapter 13, does my city, borough, town or port keep its liberties and free customs?
GIVEN `it is a city, borough, town or port other than London` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a city, borough, town or port other than London?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 13, does my city, borough, town or port keep its liberties and free customs` IS
    `ch 13 -- all other cities, boroughs, towns and ports have all their liberties and free customs` `it is a city, borough, town or port other than London`

-- Chapter 14.  Fork F14: forty elapsed days is taken to be enough.
@export Under chapter 14, was the summons for the common counsel made as the Charter requires?
GIVEN `the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons were summoned by letters under seal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons were summoned by letters under seal?
      `all other tenants in chief were summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that all other tenants in chief were summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs?
      `the days between the summons and the date fixed` IS A NUMBER @desc How many days were there between the summons and the date fixed?
      `a place was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a place was fixed?
      `every letter of summons specified the reason` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that every letter of summons specified the reason?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 14, was the summons for the common counsel made as the Charter requires` IS
    `ch 14 -- the summons for the common counsel is as the Charter requires` `the archbishops, bishops, abbots, earls and greater barons were summoned by letters under seal` `all other tenants in chief were summoned generally through the sheriffs and bailiffs` `the days between the summons and the date fixed` `a place was fixed` `every letter of summons specified the reason`

-- Chapter 14.
@export Under chapter 14, does the business proceed on the day appointed even if not all who were summoned have come?
GIVEN `the summons has been made as the Charter requires` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the summons has been made as the Charter requires?
      `not all who were summoned have come` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that not all who were summoned have come?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 14, does the business proceed on the day appointed even if not all who were summoned have come` IS
    `ch 14 -- the business proceeds on the day appointed according to the counsel of those present` `the summons has been made as the Charter requires` `not all who were summoned have come`

-- Chapter 15.
@export Under chapter 15, may the King license my lord to take an aid from me?
GIVEN `what the aid is for` IS AidPurpose @desc Is it for ransoming the King, making his eldest son a knight, marrying his eldest daughter (once), or some other purpose?
      `an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 15, may the King license my lord to take an aid from me` IS
    `ch 15 -- the King may grant a licence to take an aid from a lord's own free tenants` `what the aid is for` `an aid for the marriage of the King's eldest daughter has been levied before`

-- Chapter 15.
@export Under chapter 15, may my lord take this aid from me?
GIVEN `what the aid is for` IS AidPurpose @desc Is it for ransoming the lord, making his eldest son a knight, marrying his eldest daughter (once), or some other purpose?
      `an aid for the marriage of the lord's eldest daughter has been levied before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an aid for the marriage of the lord's eldest daughter has been levied before?
      `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the aid is no more than a reasonable aid?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 15, may my lord take this aid from me` IS
    `ch 15 -- the aid levied by a lord on one of the three occasions may be this aid` `what the aid is for` `an aid for the marriage of the lord's eldest daughter has been levied before` `the aid is no more than a reasonable aid`

-- Chapter 16.  The amounts are in whatever unit the service is measured.
@export Under chapter 16, may I be made to do greater service than is due from my holding?
GIVEN `my holding is a knight's fee or another free tenement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your holding is a knight's fee or another free tenement?
      `the service demanded` IS A NUMBER @desc How much service is demanded?
      `the service due from my holding` IS A NUMBER @desc How much service is due from the holding?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 16, may I be made to do greater service than is due from my holding` IS
    `ch 16 -- greater service than is due may be demanded` `my holding is a knight's fee or another free tenement` `the service demanded` `the service due from my holding`

§§ `Courts and justice (chapters 17 to 22)`

-- Chapter 17.
@export Under chapter 17, may my common plea be heard wherever the King's court happens to be?
GIVEN `my plea is a common plea` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your plea is a common plea?
      `it is held in some fixed place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is held in some fixed place?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 17, may my common plea be heard wherever the King's court happens to be` IS
    `ch 17 -- the common plea may be held where the King's court happens to be` `my plea is a common plea` `it is held in some fixed place`

-- Chapter 18.
@export Under chapter 18, may my inquest be held here?
GIVEN `the kind of inquest` IS InquestKind @desc Is it novel disseisin, mort d'ancestor, darrein presentment, or some other kind of inquest?
      `it is held in the county court of its own county` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is held in the county court of its own county?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 18, may my inquest be held here` IS
    `ch 18 -- the inquest may be held here` `the kind of inquest` `it is held in the county court of its own county`

-- Chapter 18.
@export Under chapter 18, were the justiciars sent through my county often enough?
GIVEN `the times the justiciars were sent through my county in the year` IS A NUMBER @desc How many times in the year were the justiciars sent through your county?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 18, were the justiciars sent through my county often enough` IS
    `ch 18 -- the justiciars were sent through the county often enough` `the times the justiciars were sent through my county in the year`

-- Chapter 18.
@export Under chapter 18, are the assizes held as the Charter requires?
GIVEN `the number of justiciars` IS A NUMBER @desc How many justiciars were sent?
      `the number of knights of the county` IS A NUMBER @desc How many knights of the county sat with them?
      `the knights were chosen by the county` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the knights were chosen by the county?
      `it was held in the county court on the day and in the place of its meeting` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was held in the county court on the day and in the place of its meeting?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 18, are the assizes held as the Charter requires` IS
    `ch 18 -- the assizes are held as the Charter requires` `the number of justiciars` `the number of knights of the county` `the knights were chosen by the county` `it was held in the county court on the day and in the place of its meeting`

-- Chapter 19.
@export Under chapter 19, do enough of the knights and freeholders present remain?
GIVEN `the number of knights and freeholders who remain` IS A NUMBER @desc How many knights and freeholders remain?
      `the number required for the efficient making of judgments` IS A NUMBER @desc How many are needed to make the judgments efficiently?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 19, do enough of the knights and freeholders present remain` IS
    `ch 19 -- enough of the knights and freeholders present remain` `the number of knights and freeholders who remain` `the number required for the efficient making of judgments`

-- Chapter 19.
@export Under chapter 19, must I, a knight or freeholder who was present at the county court, remain?
GIVEN `the assize cannot be taken on the day of the county court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the assize cannot be taken on the day of the county court?
      `I was present at the county court on that day as a knight or freeholder` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were present at the county court on that day as a knight or freeholder?
      `the number already remaining is less than the number required for the efficient making of judgments` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the number already remaining is less than the number required for the efficient making of judgments?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 19, must I, a knight or freeholder who was present at the county court, remain` IS
    `ch 19 -- the knight or freeholder who was present remains` `the assize cannot be taken on the day of the county court` `I was present at the county court on that day as a knight or freeholder` `the number already remaining is less than the number required for the efficient making of judgments`

-- Chapter 20.
@export What is saved to me if I am amerced?
GIVEN `what I am` IS ClassOfPerson @desc Are you a freeman, a merchant or a villein?
GIVETH A SavedItem
DECIDE `What is saved to me if I am amerced` IS
    `ch 20 -- what is saved to a person of this class when he is amerced` `what I am`

-- Chapter 20.
@export Under chapter 20, may this amercement be imposed on me?
GIVEN `I have fallen into the King's mercy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have fallen into the King's mercy?
      `the amercement is in accordance with the degree or gravity of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amercement is in accordance with the degree or gravity of the offence?
      `the amercement leaves me what is saved to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amercement leaves you what is saved to you?
      `it is imposed by the oath of honest men of the neighbourhood` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is imposed by the oath of honest men of the neighbourhood?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 20, may this amercement be imposed on me` IS
    `ch 20 -- the amercement may be imposed` `I have fallen into the King's mercy` `the amercement is in accordance with the degree or gravity of the offence` `the amercement leaves me what is saved to me` `it is imposed by the oath of honest men of the neighbourhood`

-- Chapter 21.
@export Under chapter 21, may I, an earl or baron, be amerced in this way?
GIVEN `I am an earl or a baron` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are an earl or a baron?
      `the amercement is through my peers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amercement is through your peers?
      `the amercement is in accordance with the degree of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amercement is in accordance with the degree of the offence?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 21, may I, an earl or baron, be amerced in this way` IS
    `ch 21 -- the earl or baron may be amerced in this way` `I am an earl or a baron` `the amercement is through my peers` `the amercement is in accordance with the degree of the offence`

-- Chapter 22.
@export Under chapter 22, may I, a clerk, be amerced in this way?
GIVEN `I am a clerk` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a clerk?
      `the amercement is in respect of my lay holding` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amercement is in respect of your lay holding?
      `the amercement is after the manner of the others aforesaid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amercement is after the manner of the others aforesaid?
      `the amercement is in accordance with the extent of my church benefice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the amercement is in accordance with the extent of your church benefice?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 22, may I, a clerk, be amerced in this way` IS
    `ch 22 -- the clerk may be amerced in this way` `I am a clerk` `the amercement is in respect of my lay holding` `the amercement is after the manner of the others aforesaid` `the amercement is in accordance with the extent of my church benefice`

§§ `Exactions and the King's officers (chapters 23 to 32)`

-- Chapter 23.
@export Under chapter 23, may I be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank?
GIVEN `from of old I was legally bound to make bridges at river banks` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that from of old you were legally bound to make bridges at river banks?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 23, may I be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank` IS
    `ch 23 -- a community or individual may be compelled to make a bridge at a river bank` `from of old I was legally bound to make bridges at river banks`

-- Chapter 24.
@export Under chapter 24, may a sheriff, constable, coroner or bailiff hold pleas of the Crown?
GIVEN `the officer` IS Party @desc Who would hold the pleas: a sheriff, a constable, a coroner, a bailiff, or someone else?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 24, may a sheriff, constable, coroner or bailiff hold pleas of the Crown` IS
    `ch 24 -- the officer may hold pleas of the Crown` `the officer`

-- Chapter 25.  The amounts are in whatever unit the rent is paid in.
@export Under chapter 25, may this rent or payment be demanded of my county, hundred, wapentake or trithing?
GIVEN `the unit` IS UnitOfRent @desc Is it a county, a hundred, a wapentake, a trithing, a demesne manor or another unit?
      `the old rent` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the old rent?
      `the rent demanded` IS A NUMBER @desc What rent is demanded?
      `an additional payment is demanded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that an additional payment is demanded?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 25, may this rent or payment be demanded of my county, hundred, wapentake or trithing` IS
    `ch 25 -- the rent or payment demanded of this unit may be demanded` `the unit` `the old rent` `the rent demanded` `an additional payment is demanded`

-- Chapter 26.
@export Under chapter 26, may an officer attach and catalogue the chattels my deceased relative left, for a debt to the King?
GIVEN `the officer` IS Party @desc Is it a sheriff, a bailiff, or someone else?
      `the holder of a lay fief of the King has died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the holder of a lay fief of the King has died?
      `the officer exhibits the King's letters patent of summons for a debt which the deceased owed to the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the officer exhibits the King's letters patent of summons for a debt which the deceased owed to the King?
      `the chattels are found upon the lay fief` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the chattels are found upon the lay fief?
      `the value to be attached` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the chattels to be attached?
      `the debt owed to the King` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the debt owed to the King?
      `it is done at the sight of lawful men` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is done at the sight of lawful men?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 26, may an officer attach and catalogue the chattels my deceased relative left, for a debt to the King` IS
    `ch 26 -- the officer may attach and catalogue chattels of the deceased` `the officer` `the holder of a lay fief of the King has died` `the officer exhibits the King's letters patent of summons for a debt which the deceased owed to the King` `the chattels are found upon the lay fief` `the value to be attached` `the debt owed to the King` `it is done at the sight of lawful men`

-- Chapter 26.
@export Under chapter 26, may the attached chattels be removed from the lay fief?
GIVEN `chattels have been attached under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that chattels have been attached under this chapter?
      `the debt which is evident has been fully paid to the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the debt which is evident has been fully paid to the King?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 26, may the attached chattels be removed from the lay fief` IS
    `ch 26 -- the attached chattels may be removed from the lay fief` `chattels have been attached under this chapter` `the debt which is evident has been fully paid to the King`

-- Chapter 26.
@export How much is left to the executors after the debt to the King?
GIVEN `the value of the chattels of the deceased` IS A NUMBER @desc What is the value of the chattels of the deceased?
      `the debt which is evident` IS A NUMBER @desc How much is the debt which is evident?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How much is left to the executors after the debt to the King` IS
    `ch 26 -- the value of the residue left to the executors` `the value of the chattels of the deceased` `the debt which is evident`

-- Chapter 26.
@export Under chapter 26, do my wife and children have their reasonable shares?
GIVEN `nothing is due from the deceased to the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that nothing is due from the deceased to the King?
      `he leaves a wife or children` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that he leaves a wife or children?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 26, do my wife and children have their reasonable shares` IS
    `ch 26 -- the wife and children have their reasonable shares` `nothing is due from the deceased to the King` `he leaves a wife or children`

-- Chapter 27.
@export How are the chattels of a freeman who died intestate distributed?
GIVEN `a freeman has died intestate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a freeman has died intestate?
GIVETH A Distribution
DECIDE `How are the chattels of a freeman who died intestate distributed` IS
    `ch 27 -- how the chattels are distributed` `a freeman has died intestate`

-- Chapter 27.
@export Under chapter 27, is the debt the deceased owed me saved to me?
GIVEN `a freeman has died intestate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a freeman has died intestate?
      `the deceased owed me a debt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deceased owed you a debt?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 27, is the debt the deceased owed me saved to me` IS
    `ch 27 -- the debt which the deceased owed to a person is saved to him` `a freeman has died intestate` `the deceased owed me a debt`

-- Chapter 28.
@export Under chapter 28, may a constable or bailiff take my corn or other provisions?
GIVEN `the officer` IS Party @desc Is it a constable, a bailiff, or someone else?
      `he tenders money for it immediately` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that he tenders money for it immediately?
      `I permit postponement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you permit postponement?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 28, may a constable or bailiff take my corn or other provisions` IS
    `ch 28 -- the officer may take corn or other provisions in this way` `the officer` `he tenders money for it immediately` `I permit postponement`

-- Chapter 29.
@export Under chapter 29, may a constable compel me, a knight, to give money in lieu of castle-guard?
GIVEN `the officer` IS Party @desc Is it a constable, or someone else?
      `I am willing to perform the guard in my own person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are willing to perform the guard in your own person?
      `I cannot do it myself from any reasonable cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you cannot do it yourself from any reasonable cause?
      `another responsible man will perform it for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that another responsible man will perform it for you?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 29, may a constable compel me, a knight, to give money in lieu of castle-guard` IS
    `ch 29 -- the constable may compel the knight to give money in lieu of castle-guard` `the officer` `I am willing to perform the guard in my own person` `I cannot do it myself from any reasonable cause` `another responsible man will perform it for me`

-- Chapter 29.
@export Under chapter 29, am I relieved from guard in proportion to the time I was on service for the King?
GIVEN `the King has led or sent me upon military service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King has led or sent you upon military service?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 29, am I relieved from guard in proportion to the time I was on service for the King` IS
    `ch 29 -- the knight is relieved from guard in proportion to his time on service` `the King has led or sent me upon military service`

-- Chapter 29.  The text says "in proportion" and states no proportion (finding).
@export For how many days of guard am I relieved?
GIVEN `the days I have been on service because of the King` IS A NUMBER @desc For how many days have you been on service because of the King?
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `For how many days of guard am I relieved` IS
    `ch 29 -- the days of guard of which the knight is relieved` `the days I have been on service because of the King`

-- Chapter 30.
@export Under chapter 30, may my horses or carts be taken for transport duty?
GIVEN `the horses or carts belong to a freeman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the horses or carts belong to a freeman?
      `I do not agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you do not agree?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 30, may my horses or carts be taken for transport duty` IS
    `ch 30 -- horses or carts may be taken for transport duty` `the horses or carts belong to a freeman` `I do not agree`

-- Chapter 31.
@export Under chapter 31, may the King or his bailiffs take my wood for his castles or other work?
GIVEN `who would take it` IS Party @desc Is it the King, a bailiff, or someone else?
      `the wood is not the King's` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the wood is not the King's?
      `I do not agree` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you do not agree?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 31, may the King or his bailiffs take my wood for his castles or other work` IS
    `ch 31 -- wood may be taken for the King's castles or other work` `who would take it` `the wood is not the King's` `I do not agree`

-- Chapter 32.  The text does not say from what day it is counted (fork F32), so the person states it.  The years in the cases are arbitrary.
@export Until what day may the King keep the lands of a person convicted of felony?
GIVEN `the day of the month from which the year and a day is counted` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month does the year and a day begin to run?
      `the month from which the year and a day is counted` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month (1 to 12)?
      `the year from which the year and a day is counted` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `Until what day may the King keep the lands of a person convicted of felony` IS
    `ch 32 -- the last day the King may retain the lands` `the starting day`
    WHERE
        `the starting day` MEANS Date `the day of the month from which the year and a day is counted` `the month from which the year and a day is counted` `the year from which the year and a day is counted`

-- Chapter 32.
@export Under chapter 32, may the King keep my lands on this day?
GIVEN `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the lands are those of a person convicted of felony?
      `the starting day, day of the month` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month does the year and a day begin to run?
      `the starting day, month` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the starting day, year` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
      `the day in question, day of the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What day of the month is the day in question?
      `the day in question, month` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the day in question, year` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 32, may the King keep my lands on this day` IS
    `ch 32 -- the King may retain the lands on this day` `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony` `the starting day` `the day in question`
    WHERE
        `the starting day` MEANS Date `the starting day, day of the month` `the starting day, month` `the starting day, year`
        `the day in question` MEANS Date `the day in question, day of the month` `the day in question, month` `the day in question, year`

-- Chapter 32.
@export Under chapter 32, must the lands be handed over to the lords of the fiefs by this day?
GIVEN `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the lands are those of a person convicted of felony?
      `the starting day, day of the month` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month does the year and a day begin to run?
      `the starting day, month` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the starting day, year` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
      `the day in question, day of the month` IS A NUMBER @desc What day of the month is the day in question?
      `the day in question, month` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the day in question, year` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 32, must the lands be handed over to the lords of the fiefs by this day` IS
    `ch 32 -- the lands are handed over to the lords of the fiefs` `the lands are those of a person convicted of felony` `the starting day` `the day in question`
    WHERE
        `the starting day` MEANS Date `the starting day, day of the month` `the starting day, month` `the starting day, year`
        `the day in question` MEANS Date `the day in question, day of the month` `the day in question, month` `the day in question, year`

§§ `Kydells, writs, measures and wardship (chapters 33 to 38)`

-- Chapter 33.  "Kydell" is not defined by the text.
@export Under chapter 33, must the kydell be removed?
GIVEN `the kydell is in England` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the kydell is in England?
      `the kydell is upon the sea coast` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the kydell is upon the sea coast?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 33, must the kydell be removed` IS
    `ch 33 -- the kydell is to be removed` `the kydell is in England` `the kydell is upon the sea coast`

-- Chapter 34.
@export Under chapter 34, may the writ praecipe be issued concerning my tenement?
GIVEN `the writ is the writ called praecipe` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the writ is the writ called praecipe?
      `the writ concerns a tenement whereby a freeman may lose his court` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the writ concerns a tenement whereby a freeman may lose his court?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 34, may the writ praecipe be issued concerning my tenement` IS
    `ch 34 -- the writ praecipe may be issued` `the writ is the writ called praecipe` `the writ concerns a tenement whereby a freeman may lose his court`

-- Chapter 35.
@export What measure or weight applies to what I sell?
GIVEN `what I sell` IS Commodity @desc Is it wine, ale, corn, cloth (dyed, russet or halberget), a weight, or something else?
GIVETH A Standard
DECIDE `What measure or weight applies to what I sell` IS
    `ch 35 -- the standard throughout the realm` `what I sell`

-- Chapter 35.
@export Under chapter 35, may a measure other than the standard be used for what I sell?
GIVEN `what I sell` IS Commodity @desc Is it wine, ale, corn, cloth (dyed, russet or halberget), a weight, or something else?
      `the sale is within the realm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the sale is within the realm?
      `the measure used differs from the standard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the measure used differs from the standard?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 35, may a measure other than the standard be used for what I sell` IS
    `ch 35 -- a measure other than the standard may be used` `what I sell` `the sale is within the realm` `the measure used differs from the standard`

-- Chapter 36.
@export Under chapter 36, may I be charged for the writ of inquisition of life or limbs?
GIVEN `the writ is a writ of inquisition of life or limbs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the writ is a writ of inquisition of life or limbs?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 36, may I be charged for the writ of inquisition of life or limbs` IS
    `ch 36 -- something may be given or taken for the writ` `the writ is a writ of inquisition of life or limbs`

-- Chapter 36.
@export Under chapter 36, may the writ of inquisition of life or limbs be denied to me?
GIVEN `the writ is a writ of inquisition of life or limbs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the writ is a writ of inquisition of life or limbs?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 36, may the writ of inquisition of life or limbs be denied to me` IS
    `ch 36 -- the writ may be denied` `the writ is a writ of inquisition of life or limbs`

-- Chapter 37.
@export Under chapter 37, may the King have wardship of my heir or my land by reason of my tenure?
GIVEN `my tenure from the King` IS TenureOfKing @desc Do you hold of the King by fee-farm, socage, burgage, petty serjeanty (rendering knives, arrows or the like), or some other tenure?
      `what the wardship would be of` IS WardshipOf @desc Is it wardship of your heir, of your land held of another lord by knight's service, or of the fee-farm, socage or burgage itself?
      `I hold also land of another lord by knight's service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you hold also land of another lord by knight's service?
      `my fee-farm, socage or burgage owes knight's service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that your fee-farm, socage or burgage owes knight's service?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 37, may the King have wardship of my heir or my land by reason of my tenure` IS
    `ch 37 -- the King may have wardship of this by reason of the tenure` `my tenure from the King` `what the wardship would be of` `I hold also land of another lord by knight's service` `my fee-farm, socage or burgage owes knight's service`

-- Chapter 38.
@export Under chapter 38, may a bailiff put me to my law on his own mere word of mouth?
GIVEN `the officer` IS Party @desc Is it a bailiff, or someone else?
      `credible witnesses are brought for this purpose` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that credible witnesses are brought for this purpose?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 38, may a bailiff put me to my law on his own mere word of mouth` IS
    `ch 38 -- the officer may put a man to his law upon his own mere word of mouth` `the officer` `credible witnesses are brought for this purpose`

§§ `Judgment, right and justice, merchants and travellers (chapters 39 to 42)`

-- Chapter 39.  The translation says "and": both are needed (fork F39a).  Who does it is not named for the passive limb (fork F39d).
@export Under chapter 39, may the King imprison me or take my land without a judgment of my peers?
GIVEN `I am a freeman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a freeman?
      `it is done by the lawful judgment of my peers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is done by the lawful judgment of your peers?
      `it is done by the law of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is done by the law of the land?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 39, may the King imprison me or take my land without a judgment of my peers` IS
    `ch 39 -- a freeman may be arrested, detained in prison, deprived of his freehold, outlawed, banished or in any way molested` `I am a freeman` `it is done by the lawful judgment of my peers` `it is done by the law of the land`

-- Chapter 40.  "To no one": the person need not be a freeman (fork F40a).
@export Under chapter 40, may the King sell, refuse or delay right or justice to me?
GIVEN `what is withheld is right or justice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that what is withheld is right or justice?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 40, may the King sell, refuse or delay right or justice to me` IS
    `ch 40 -- right or justice may be sold, refused or delayed` `what is withheld is right or justice`

-- Chapter 41.
@export Under chapter 41, do I, a merchant, have safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and water?
GIVEN `I am a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a merchant?
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a time of war?
      `I am of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are of the land at war with the King?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 41, do I, a merchant, have safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and water` IS
    `ch 41 -- the merchant has safe and secure exit, entry, stay and movement by land and by water` `I am a merchant` `it is a time of war` `I am of the land at war with the King`

-- Chapter 41.
@export Under chapter 41, may I, a merchant, buy and sell?
GIVEN `I am a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a merchant?
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a time of war?
      `I am of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are of the land at war with the King?
      `the buying and selling is by the ancient and right customs` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the buying and selling is by the ancient and right customs?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 41, may I, a merchant, buy and sell` IS
    `ch 41 -- the merchant may buy and sell` `I am a merchant` `it is a time of war` `I am of the land at war with the King` `the buying and selling is by the ancient and right customs`

-- Chapter 41.
@export Under chapter 41, may a toll be taken from me, a merchant?
GIVEN `I am a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a merchant?
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a time of war?
      `I am of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are of the land at war with the King?
      `the toll is an evil toll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the toll is an evil toll?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 41, may a toll be taken from me, a merchant` IS
    `ch 41 -- a toll may be taken from the merchant` `I am a merchant` `it is a time of war` `I am of the land at war with the King` `the toll is an evil toll`

-- Chapter 41.
@export Under chapter 41, am I, a merchant of a land at war with the King, to be detained?
GIVEN `I am a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a merchant?
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a time of war?
      `I am of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are of the land at war with the King?
      `I was found in the land at the beginning of the war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were found in the land at the beginning of the war?
      `information has been received by the King or his chief justiciar of how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that information has been received by the King or his chief justiciar of how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 41, am I, a merchant of a land at war with the King, to be detained` IS
    `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is to be detained` `I am a merchant` `it is a time of war` `I am of the land at war with the King` `I was found in the land at the beginning of the war` `information has been received by the King or his chief justiciar of how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated`

-- Chapter 41.
@export Under chapter 41, may my body or goods be injured while I am detained?
