      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a time of war?
      `I am of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are of the land at war with the King?
      `I was found in the land at the beginning of the war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were found in the land at the beginning of the war?
      `information has been received by the King or his chief justiciar of how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that information has been received by the King or his chief justiciar of how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 41, may my body or goods be injured while I am detained` IS
    `ch 41 -- the body or goods of the detained merchant may be injured` `I am a merchant` `it is a time of war` `I am of the land at war with the King` `I was found in the land at the beginning of the war` `information has been received by the King or his chief justiciar of how the merchants of our land found in the land at war with us are treated`

-- Chapter 41.
@export Under chapter 41, am I, a merchant of a land at war with the King, safe in the kingdom?
GIVEN `I am a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a merchant?
      `it is a time of war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a time of war?
      `I am of the land at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are of the land at war with the King?
      `I was found in the land at the beginning of the war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were found in the land at the beginning of the war?
      `the merchants of our land are safe in the land at war with us` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the merchants of our land are safe in the land at war with us?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 41, am I, a merchant of a land at war with the King, safe in the kingdom` IS
    `ch 41 -- the enemy merchant is safe in our land` `I am a merchant` `it is a time of war` `I am of the land at war with the King` `I was found in the land at the beginning of the war` `the merchants of our land are safe in the land at war with us`

-- Chapter 42.
@export Under chapter 42, may I leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water?
GIVEN `I am imprisoned or outlawed in accordance with the law of the kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are imprisoned or outlawed in accordance with the law of the kingdom?
      `I am a native of a country at war with the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a native of a country at war with the King?
      `I am a merchant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a merchant?
      `it is a short period in time of war` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is a short period in time of war?
      `the restriction is on grounds of public policy` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the restriction is on grounds of public policy?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 42, may I leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` IS
    `ch 42 -- the person may leave the kingdom and return, safe and secure by land and water` `I am imprisoned or outlawed in accordance with the law of the kingdom` `I am a native of a country at war with the King` `I am a merchant` `it is a short period in time of war` `the restriction is on grounds of public policy`

-- Chapter 42.
@export Under chapter 42, do I still owe the King allegiance when I leave?
GIVEN `I owe allegiance to the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you owe allegiance to the King?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 42, do I still owe the King allegiance when I leave` IS
    `ch 42 -- the allegiance due to the King remains owed` `I owe allegiance to the King`

§§ `Escheats, the forest, officers and abbeys (chapters 43 to 48)`

-- Chapter 43.  The amounts are in whatever unit the relief is paid in.
@export Under chapter 43, may the King take this relief and service from me, the heir of one who held of an escheat?
GIVEN `the deceased held of an escheat which is in the King's hands and is a barony` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the deceased held of an escheat which is in the King's hands and is a barony?
      `the relief the King would take from me` IS A NUMBER @desc What relief would the King take?
      `the relief I would have given the baron if the barony had been in the baron's hand` IS A NUMBER @desc What relief would you have given the baron?
      `the King would require a service the baron would not have had` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King would require a service the baron would not have had?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 43, may the King take this relief and service from me, the heir of one who held of an escheat` IS
    `ch 43 -- the King may take this relief and service from the heir` `the deceased held of an escheat which is in the King's hands and is a barony` `the relief the King would take from me` `the relief I would have given the baron if the barony had been in the baron's hand` `the King would require a service the baron would not have had`

-- Chapter 43.
@export Under chapter 43, must the King hold the escheat in the manner in which the baron held it?
GIVEN `the escheat is in the King's hands and is a barony` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the escheat is in the King's hands and is a barony?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 43, must the King hold the escheat in the manner in which the baron held it` IS
    `ch 43 -- the King holds the escheat in the manner in which the baron held it` `the escheat is in the King's hands and is a barony`

-- Chapter 44.
@export Under chapter 44, must I come before the justiciars of the forest upon a general summons?
GIVEN `I dwell without the forest` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you dwell without the forest?
      `I am impleaded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are impleaded?
      `I have become surety for a person attached for forest offences` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have become surety for a person attached for forest offences?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 44, must I come before the justiciars of the forest upon a general summons` IS
    `ch 44 -- the man must come before the justiciars of the forest upon a general summons` `I dwell without the forest` `I am impleaded` `I have become surety for a person attached for forest offences`

-- Chapter 45.
@export Under chapter 45, may the King appoint this person as justice, constable, sheriff or bailiff?
GIVEN `the office` IS OfficeKind @desc Is the office a justice, a constable, a sheriff, a bailiff, or some other?
      `the person knows the law of the realm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person knows the law of the realm?
      `the person means to observe it well` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the person means to observe it well?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 45, may the King appoint this person as justice, constable, sheriff or bailiff` IS
    `ch 45 -- the King may appoint this person to the office` `the office` `the person knows the law of the realm` `the person means to observe it well`

-- Chapter 46.
@export Under chapter 46, do I, a baron who founded an abbey, have its wardship when it is vacant?
GIVEN `I am a baron` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a baron?
      `I founded the abbey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you founded the abbey?
      `I hold charters from the kings of England concerning the abbey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you hold charters from the kings of England concerning the abbey?
      `I have long-continued possession of the abbey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have long-continued possession of the abbey?
      `the abbey is vacant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the abbey is vacant?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 46, do I, a baron who founded an abbey, have its wardship when it is vacant` IS
    `ch 46 -- the baron shall have the wardship of the abbey` `I am a baron` `I founded the abbey` `I hold charters from the kings of England concerning the abbey` `I have long-continued possession of the abbey` `the abbey is vacant`

-- Chapter 47.
@export Under chapter 47, is a forest made a forest in the King's time to be disafforested?
GIVEN `the forest was made a forest in the King's time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the forest was made a forest in the King's time?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 47, is a forest made a forest in the King's time to be disafforested` IS
    `ch 47 -- the forest is to be disafforested` `the forest was made a forest in the King's time`

-- Chapter 47.
@export Under chapter 47, is a river-bank placed in defence in the King's time to be released?
GIVEN `the river-bank was placed in defence by the King in his time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the river-bank was placed in defence by the King in his time?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 47, is a river-bank placed in defence in the King's time to be released` IS
    `ch 47 -- the river-bank is to be released from defence` `the river-bank was placed in defence by the King in his time`

-- Chapter 48.  Fork F48a: the proviso governs the inquiry and the abolition.
@export Under chapter 48, is an evil custom of the forest to be inquired into?
GIVEN `the custom is an evil custom connected with forests and warrens, foresters and warreners, sheriffs and their officers, river-banks and their wardens` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the custom is an evil custom connected with forests and warrens, foresters and warreners, sheriffs and their officers, river-banks and their wardens?
      `the King, or his justiciar if the King is not in England, has previously had intimation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King, or his justiciar if the King is not in England, has previously had intimation?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 48, is an evil custom of the forest to be inquired into` IS
    `ch 48 -- the evil custom is to be inquired into` `the custom is an evil custom connected with forests and warrens, foresters and warreners, sheriffs and their officers, river-banks and their wardens` `the King, or his justiciar if the King is not in England, has previously had intimation`

-- Chapter 48.
@export Under chapter 48, is the evil custom to be utterly abolished?
GIVEN `the custom is an evil custom connected with forests and warrens, foresters and warreners, sheriffs and their officers, river-banks and their wardens` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the custom is an evil custom connected with forests and warrens, foresters and warreners, sheriffs and their officers, river-banks and their wardens?
      `the King, or his justiciar if the King is not in England, has previously had intimation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King, or his justiciar if the King is not in England, has previously had intimation?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 48, is the evil custom to be utterly abolished` IS
    `ch 48 -- the evil custom is to be utterly abolished` `the custom is an evil custom connected with forests and warrens, foresters and warreners, sheriffs and their officers, river-banks and their wardens` `the King, or his justiciar if the King is not in England, has previously had intimation`

-- Chapter 48.
@export Under chapter 48, is the inquest into the evil customs of the forest made up as the text requires?
GIVEN `the number of knights` IS A NUMBER @desc How many knights are on the inquest?
      `they are sworn` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they are sworn?
      `they are knights of the same county` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they are knights of the same county?
      `they were chosen by the honest men of the same county` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they were chosen by the honest men of the same county?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 48, is the inquest into the evil customs of the forest made up as the text requires` IS
    `ch 48 -- the inquest is constituted as the text requires` `the number of knights` `they are sworn` `they are knights of the same county` `they were chosen by the honest men of the same county`

-- Chapter 48.  The years in the cases are arbitrary.  Fork F48b: the day of the inquest is not counted.
@export By what day must the evil custom be abolished?
GIVEN `the day of the month of the inquest` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the inquest?
      `the month of the inquest` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the year of the inquest` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the evil custom be abolished` IS
    `ch 48 -- the last day for abolishing the evil custom` `the day of the inquest`
    WHERE
        `the day of the inquest` MEANS Date `the day of the month of the inquest` `the month of the inquest` `the year of the inquest`

-- Chapter 48.
@export Under chapter 48, was the evil custom abolished within the forty days?
GIVEN `the day of the month of the inquest` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the inquest?
      `the month of the inquest` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the year of the inquest` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
      `the day of the month of the abolition` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was it abolished?
      `the month of the abolition` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the year of the abolition` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 48, was the evil custom abolished within the forty days` IS
    `ch 48 -- abolition on this day is within the forty days` `the day of the inquest` `the day of abolition`
    WHERE
        `the day of the inquest` MEANS Date `the day of the month of the inquest` `the month of the inquest` `the year of the inquest`
        `the day of abolition` MEANS Date `the day of the month of the abolition` `the month of the abolition` `the year of the abolition`

-- Chapter 48.
@export Under chapter 48, may an evil custom that has been abolished be restored?
GIVEN `the custom has been abolished under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the custom has been abolished under this chapter?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 48, may an evil custom that has been abolished be restored` IS
    `ch 48 -- the abolished custom may be restored` `the custom has been abolished under this chapter`

§§ `Restitution, respite and the Welsh and Scots (chapters 49 to 59)`

-- Chapter 49.
@export Under chapter 49, are the hostages and charters I delivered to the King to be restored?
GIVEN `they were delivered to the King by Englishmen` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they were delivered to the King by Englishmen?
      `they are hostages or charters` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they are hostages or charters?
      `they were delivered as sureties of the peace or of faithful service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that they were delivered as sureties of the peace or of faithful service?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 49, are the hostages and charters I delivered to the King to be restored` IS
    `ch 49 -- the hostages and charters are to be restored` `they were delivered to the King by Englishmen` `they are hostages or charters` `they were delivered as sureties of the peace or of faithful service`

-- Chapter 50.
@export Under chapter 50, am I one of those to be removed from my bailiwick and barred from one in future?
GIVEN `who I am` IS NamedRelation @desc Are you one of the persons the Charter names as relations of Gerard de Athyes (or a brother, the nephew or the brood), or someone not named?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 50, am I one of those to be removed from my bailiwick and barred from one in future` IS
    `ch 50 -- the person is to be removed from his bailiwick` `who I am`

-- Chapter 50.
@export Under chapter 50, may I, one of those named, hold a bailiwick in England in future?
GIVEN `who I am` IS NamedRelation @desc Are you one of the persons the Charter names as relations of Gerard de Athyes (or a brother, the nephew or the brood), or someone not named?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 50, may I, one of those named, hold a bailiwick in England in future` IS
    `ch 50 -- the person may have a bailiwick in England in future` `who I am`

-- Chapter 51.
@export Under chapter 51, am I, a foreign-born soldier who came to the kingdom's hurt, to be banished?
GIVEN `peace is restored` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that peace is restored?
      `what I am` IS ForeignForce @desc Are you a knight, a cross-bowman, a serjeant, a mercenary soldier, or something else?
      `I am foreign-born` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are foreign-born?
      `I came with horses and arms to the kingdom's hurt` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you came with horses and arms to the kingdom's hurt?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 51, am I, a foreign-born soldier who came to the kingdom's hurt, to be banished` IS
    `ch 51 -- the person is to be banished from the kingdom` `peace is restored` `what I am` `I am foreign-born` `I came with horses and arms to the kingdom's hurt`

-- Chapter 52.
@export Under chapter 52, must the King restore what he took from me without the judgment of my peers?
GIVEN `I was dispossessed or removed by the King from my lands, castles, franchises or right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you were dispossessed or removed by the King from your lands, castles, franchises or right?
      `it was without the legal judgment of my peers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was without the legal judgment of your peers?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 52, must the King restore what he took from me without the judgment of my peers` IS
    `ch 52 -- the lands, castles, franchises or right are to be restored` `I was dispossessed or removed by the King from my lands, castles, franchises or right` `it was without the legal judgment of my peers`

-- Chapter 52.
@export Who decides a dispute over the restoration?
GIVEN `a dispute has arisen over the restoration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a dispute has arisen over the restoration?
GIVETH A Forum
DECIDE `Who decides a dispute over the restoration` IS
    `ch 52 -- who decides a dispute over the restoration` `a dispute has arisen over the restoration`

-- Chapter 52.  "The usual term of crusaders" is taken as a plain fact.
@export Under chapter 52, does the King have respite for what his father or brother took from me?
GIVEN `the possession was taken without the lawful judgment of my peers by King Henry or by King Richard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the possession was taken without the lawful judgment of your peers by King Henry or by King Richard?
      `the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it?
      `a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross?
      `the usual term of crusaders has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the usual term of crusaders has ended?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 52, does the King have respite for what his father or brother took from me` IS
    `ch 52 -- the King has respite for the possession` `the possession was taken without the lawful judgment of my peers by King Henry or by King Richard` `the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it` `a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross` `the usual term of crusaders has ended`

-- Chapter 52.
@export Under chapter 52, must the King now grant full justice for the possession his father or brother took?
GIVEN `the possession was taken without the lawful judgment of my peers by King Henry or by King Richard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the possession was taken without the lawful judgment of your peers by King Henry or by King Richard?
      `the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it?
      `a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross?
      `the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 52, must the King now grant full justice for the possession his father or brother took` IS
    `ch 52 -- full justice is to be granted for the possession` `the possession was taken without the lawful judgment of my peers by King Henry or by King Richard` `the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it` `a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross` `the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it`

-- Chapter 53.
@export Under chapter 53, does the King have the same respite for the forests, wardships and abbeys of chapter 53?
GIVEN `the matter` IS Matter53 @desc Is it the forests Henry or Richard afforested, wardship of lands of another's fief, abbeys founded on other fiefs, or some other matter?
      `the usual term of crusaders has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the usual term of crusaders has ended?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 53, does the King have the same respite for the forests, wardships and abbeys of chapter 53` IS
    `ch 53 -- the King has the same respite concerning the matter` `the matter` `the usual term of crusaders has ended`

-- Chapter 53.
@export Under chapter 53, must the King grant me full justice for what I complain of in chapter 53?
GIVEN `the matter` IS Matter53 @desc Is it the forests Henry or Richard afforested, wardship of lands of another's fief, abbeys founded on other fiefs, or some other matter?
      `the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it?
      `I complain of the matter` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you complain of the matter?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 53, must the King grant me full justice for what I complain of in chapter 53` IS
    `ch 53 -- full justice is to be granted to the person who complains` `the matter` `the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it` `I complain of the matter`

-- Chapter 54.
@export Under chapter 54, may I be arrested or imprisoned upon the appeal of a woman?
GIVEN `the appeal is made by a woman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the appeal is made by a woman?
      `it is for the death of her husband` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it is for the death of her husband?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 54, may I be arrested or imprisoned upon the appeal of a woman` IS
    `ch 54 -- a person may be arrested or imprisoned upon the appeal` `the appeal is made by a woman` `it is for the death of her husband`

-- Chapter 55.  "Unjustly" is the person's own statement.
@export What is done with a fine or amercement I paid unjustly?
GIVEN `the fine or amercement was made or imposed unjustly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fine or amercement was made or imposed unjustly?
      `it was against the law of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was against the law of the land?
GIVETH A Remedy
DECIDE `What is done with a fine or amercement I paid unjustly` IS
    `ch 55 -- what is to be done with the fine or amercement` `the fine or amercement was made or imposed unjustly` `it was against the law of the land`

-- Chapter 55.
@export Who decides what is done with that fine or amercement?
GIVEN `the fine or amercement was made or imposed unjustly` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the fine or amercement was made or imposed unjustly?
      `it was against the law of the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was against the law of the land?
      `the archbishop of Canterbury can be present` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the archbishop of Canterbury can be present?
GIVETH A Forum
DECIDE `Who decides what is done with that fine or amercement` IS
    `ch 55 -- who decides what is done with the fine or amercement` `the fine or amercement was made or imposed unjustly` `it was against the law of the land` `the archbishop of Canterbury can be present`

-- Chapter 56.
@export Under chapter 56, I am a Welshman: must the King restore to me what he took without the judgment of my peers?
GIVEN `I am a Welshman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a Welshman?
      `the King disseised or removed me from lands, liberties or other things` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King disseised or removed you from lands, liberties or other things?
      `it was without the legal judgment of my peers in England or in Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was without the legal judgment of your peers in England or in Wales?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 56, I am a Welshman: must the King restore to me what he took without the judgment of my peers` IS
    `ch 56 -- the lands, liberties or other things are to be restored to the Welshman` `I am a Welshman` `the King disseised or removed me from lands, liberties or other things` `it was without the legal judgment of my peers in England or in Wales`

-- Chapter 56.
@export Who decides a dispute over what is restored to the Welshman?
GIVEN `a dispute has arisen over the restoration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a dispute has arisen over the restoration?
GIVETH A Forum
DECIDE `Who decides a dispute over what is restored to the Welshman` IS
    `ch 56 -- who decides a dispute over the restoration to the Welshman` `a dispute has arisen over the restoration`

-- Chapter 56.
@export By what law is a dispute over a tenement decided?
GIVEN `where the tenement lies` IS PlaceOfTenement @desc Does it lie in England, in Wales, in the marches, or elsewhere?
GIVETH A LawApplied
DECIDE `By what law is a dispute over a tenement decided` IS
    `ch 56 -- the law by which the dispute over a tenement is decided` `where the tenement lies`

-- Chapter 56.  Fork F56: "Welshmen shall do the same to us and ours" is read as the same restoration.
@export Under chapter 56, I am a Welshman: must I restore to the King and his men what I took without the judgment of their peers?
GIVEN `I am a Welshman` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a Welshman?
      `I disseised or removed the King or his men from lands, liberties or other things` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you disseised or removed the King or his men from lands, liberties or other things?
      `it was without the legal judgment of their peers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was without the legal judgment of their peers?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 56, I am a Welshman: must I restore to the King and his men what I took without the judgment of their peers` IS
    `ch 56 -- the Welshman is to restore to the King and his men` `I am a Welshman` `I disseised or removed the King or his men from lands, liberties or other things` `it was without the legal judgment of their peers`

-- Chapter 57.
@export Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: does the King have respite for what his father or brother took from me?
GIVEN `the possession was taken from a Welshman without the lawful judgment of his peers by King Henry or by King Richard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the possession was taken from a Welshman without the lawful judgment of his peers by King Henry or by King Richard?
      `the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it?
      `a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross?
      `the usual term of crusaders has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the usual term of crusaders has ended?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: does the King have respite for what his father or brother took from me` IS
    `ch 57 -- the King has respite for the possession taken from a Welshman` `the possession was taken from a Welshman without the lawful judgment of his peers by King Henry or by King Richard` `the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it` `a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross` `the usual term of crusaders has ended`

-- Chapter 57.
@export Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: must the King now grant full justice by the laws of the Welsh?
GIVEN `the possession was taken from a Welshman without the lawful judgment of his peers by King Henry or by King Richard` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the possession was taken from a Welshman without the lawful judgment of his peers by King Henry or by King Richard?
      `the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it?
      `a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross?
      `the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 57, I am a Welshman: must the King now grant full justice by the laws of the Welsh` IS
    `ch 57 -- full justice is to be granted in accordance with the laws of the Welsh` `the possession was taken from a Welshman without the lawful judgment of his peers by King Henry or by King Richard` `the King retains it in his hand, or others to whom he is bound to warrant it possess it` `a plea was raised, or an inquest made by the King's order, before he took the cross` `the King has returned from his expedition or has desisted from it`

-- Chapter 58.
@export Under chapter 58, am I, the son of Llywelyn, a hostage of Wales, or a charter of the peace, to be given up?
GIVEN `what is to be given up` IS ThingToGiveUp @desc Is it the son of Llywelyn, a hostage of Wales, a charter delivered to the King as security for the peace, or something else?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 58, am I, the son of Llywelyn, a hostage of Wales, or a charter of the peace, to be given up` IS
    `ch 58 -- the person or thing is to be given up` `what is to be given up`

-- Chapter 59.
@export I am Alexander, King of Scots: how will the King deal with the return of my sisters and hostages, my franchises and my right?
GIVEN `it concerns the return of my sisters or hostages, or my franchises, or my right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it concerns the return of your sisters or hostages, or your franchises, or your right?
      `the charters held from William my father provide otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the charters held from William your father provide otherwise?
GIVETH A Treatment
DECIDE `I am Alexander, King of Scots: how will the King deal with the return of my sisters and hostages, my franchises and my right` IS
    `ch 59 -- how the King deals with Alexander, King of Scots` `it concerns the return of my sisters or hostages, or my franchises, or my right` `the charters held from William my father provide otherwise`

-- Chapter 59.
@export Who judges the matter between the King of Scots and the King?
GIVEN `it concerns the return of the King of Scots' sisters or hostages, or his franchises, or his right` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it concerns the return of the King of Scots' sisters or hostages, or his franchises, or his right?
GIVETH A Forum
DECIDE `Who judges the matter between the King of Scots and the King` IS
    `ch 59 -- who judges the matter between the King and Alexander, King of Scots` `it concerns the return of the King of Scots' sisters or hostages, or his franchises, or his right`

§§ `Observance, the security of the barons, remission and the enjoining clause (chapters 60 to 63)`

-- Chapter 60.
@export Under chapter 60, must I observe these customs and liberties towards my men?
GIVEN `I am of the kingdom, clergy or lay` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are of the kingdom, clergy or lay?
      `I have men` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you have men?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 60, must I observe these customs and liberties towards my men` IS
    `ch 60 -- the person must observe the customs and liberties towards his men` `I am of the kingdom, clergy or lay` `I have men`

-- Chapter 61.  Fork F61a: "our justiciar" is read as the King's chief justiciar.
@export To whom do the four barons repair with an offence against the peace?
GIVEN `the King is out of the realm` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the King is out of the realm?
GIVETH A Party
DECIDE `To whom do the four barons repair with an offence against the peace` IS
    `ch 61 -- to whom the four barons repair` `the King is out of the realm`

-- Chapter 61.  The years in the cases are arbitrary.  Fork F61b: the day of intimation is not counted.
@export By what day must the transgression be corrected?
GIVEN `the day of the month it was intimated` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the transgression intimated to the King?
      `the month it was intimated` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the year it was intimated` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By what day must the transgression be corrected` IS
    `ch 61 -- the last day for correcting the transgression` `the day the transgression was intimated`
    WHERE
        `the day the transgression was intimated` MEANS Date `the day of the month it was intimated` `the month it was intimated` `the year it was intimated`

-- Chapter 61.
@export Under chapter 61, must the four barons now refer the matter to the rest of the twenty-five?
GIVEN `the day of the month it was intimated` IS A NUMBER @desc On what day of the month was the transgression intimated?
      `the month it was intimated` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the year it was intimated` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
      `the day of the month in question` IS A NUMBER @desc What is today's day of the month?
      `the month in question` IS A NUMBER @desc In what month?
      `the year in question` IS A NUMBER @desc In what year?
      `the transgression was corrected within the forty days` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the transgression was corrected within the forty days?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 61, must the four barons now refer the matter to the rest of the twenty-five` IS
    `ch 61 -- the four barons are to refer the matter to the rest of the five-and-twenty` `the day the transgression was intimated` `the day in question` `the transgression was corrected within the forty days`
    WHERE
        `the day the transgression was intimated` MEANS Date `the day of the month it was intimated` `the month it was intimated` `the year it was intimated`
        `the day in question` MEANS Date `the day of the month in question` `the month in question` `the year in question`

-- Chapter 61.  Fork F61c: "shall" is read as a duty.
@export Under chapter 61, are the five-and-twenty barons to distrain and distress the King?
GIVEN `the matter has been referred to the five-and-twenty barons` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the matter has been referred to the five-and-twenty barons?
      `redress has been obtained as they deem fit` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that redress has been obtained as they deem fit?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 61, are the five-and-twenty barons to distrain and distress the King` IS
    `ch 61 -- the five-and-twenty barons are to distrain and distress the King` `the matter has been referred to the five-and-twenty barons` `redress has been obtained as they deem fit`

-- Chapter 61.
@export Under chapter 61, may the person of the King, the queen or their children be harmed in the distraint?
GIVEN `who would be harmed` IS ProtectedPerson @desc Is it the King's own person, the queen, a child of the King, or someone else?
GIVETH A Bar
DECIDE `Under chapter 61, may the person of the King, the queen or their children be harmed in the distraint` IS
    `ch 61 -- the person may be harmed in the distraint` `who would be harmed`

-- Chapter 61.
@export Under chapter 61, do I have the King's leave to swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons?
GIVEN `I wish to swear` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you wish to swear?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 61, do I have the King's leave to swear to obey the orders of the five-and-twenty barons` IS
    `ch 61 -- the person has the King's leave to swear` `I wish to swear`

-- Chapter 61.
@export Under chapter 61, will the King compel me to swear to the twenty-five?
GIVEN `I am in the land` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are in the land?
      `of myself and of my own accord I am unwilling to swear to the twenty-five to help them in constraining and molesting the King` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that of yourself and of your own accord you are unwilling to swear to the twenty-five to help them in constraining and molesting the King?
GIVETH AN Obligation
DECIDE `Under chapter 61, will the King compel me to swear to the twenty-five` IS
    `ch 61 -- the person is to be compelled by the King's command to swear` `I am in the land` `of myself and of my own accord I am unwilling to swear to the twenty-five to help them in constraining and molesting the King`

-- Chapter 61.  Fork F61e: the text sets no quorum.
@export Under chapter 61, is what those of the twenty-five who are present ordain held as fixed and established?
GIVEN `the number of the five-and-twenty present` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of the twenty-five are present?
      `the number of those present who ordain or command it` IS A NUMBER @desc How many of those present ordain or command it?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Under chapter 61, is what those of the twenty-five who are present ordain held as fixed and established` IS
    `ch 61 -- what those present ordain or command is held as fixed and established` `the number of the five-and-twenty present` `the number of those present who ordain or command it`

-- Chapter 61.
@export What is the standing of a thing procured to revoke or diminish these concessions?
GIVEN `it was procured to revoke or diminish a part of these concessions and liberties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was procured to revoke or diminish a part of these concessions and liberties?
GIVETH A Validity
DECIDE `What is the standing of a thing procured to revoke or diminish these concessions` IS
    `ch 61 -- the thing procured` `it was procured to revoke or diminish a part of these concessions and liberties`

-- Chapter 62.
@export Under chapter 62, are the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness remitted and pardoned?
GIVEN `the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness arose between the King and his men, clergy or lay, from the date of the quarrel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness arose between the King and his men, clergy or lay, from the date of the quarrel?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 62, are the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness remitted and pardoned` IS
    `ch 62 -- the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness are remitted and pardoned` `the ill-will, hatreds and bitterness arose between the King and his men, clergy or lay, from the date of the quarrel`

-- Chapter 62.  The period's dates are not stated in the text as dates, so the person states whether it falls within.
@export Under chapter 62, is my trespass remitted and forgiven?
GIVEN `the trespass was occasioned by the said quarrel` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that the trespass was occasioned by the said quarrel?
      `it was committed from Easter in the sixteenth year of the reign till the restoration of peace` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that it was committed from Easter in the sixteenth year of the reign till the restoration of peace?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 62, is my trespass remitted and forgiven` IS
    `ch 62 -- the trespass is fully remitted and completely forgiven, as far as pertains to the King` `the trespass was occasioned by the said quarrel` `it was committed from Easter in the sixteenth year of the reign till the restoration of peace`

-- Chapter 63.
@export Under chapter 63, do I and my heirs have and hold all the liberties, rights and concessions?
GIVEN `I am a man in the kingdom, or the heir of one` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is it true that you are a man in the kingdom, or the heir of one?
GIVETH AN Entitlement
DECIDE `Under chapter 63, do I and my heirs have and hold all the liberties, rights and concessions` IS
    `ch 63 -- the person has and holds all the aforesaid liberties, rights and concessions for himself and his heirs` `I am a man in the kingdom, or the heir of one`
